---
/** /x402 — PointCast's paid HTTP receipt endpoint on Etherlink. */
import BlockLayout from '../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import {
  X402_CLIENT_EXAMPLE,
  X402_ENDPOINT,
  X402_KEYS_ENDPOINT,
  X402_TREASURY_AGENT_ID,
  X402_TREASURY_PUBLIC_KEY,
  X402_VERIFY_ENDPOINT,
} from '../lib/x402';

const EMERALD = '#0B6B3A';
const EMERALD_TINT = '#E7F3EC';
const AMBER = '#BA7517';
const INK = '#1A1A1A';
const HAIR = '#D4CBB6';
---

<BlockLayout legacy
  title="x402 — PointCast"
  description="Pay PointCast 0.01 USDC on Etherlink over x402 and receive a canonical, publicly verifiable Ed25519-signed receipt."
>
  <main class="x">
    <header class="x__header">
      <div class="x__chip">402 · AGENTS WELCOME</div>
      <h1>Pay the town, get a signed receipt</h1>
      <p class="dek">
        PointCast exposes one small paid HTTP resource for agents. Ask for it,
        receive <code>402 Payment Required</code>, pay 0.01 USDC on Etherlink
        through an off-chain Permit2 signature, and receive a countersigned
        receipt. The receipt is the product: a portable proof of the payer,
        amount, recipient, network, facilitator, and settled transaction.
      </p>
      <p class="machine"><a href="/x402.json">JSON twin →</a></p>
    </header>

    <section class="terms" aria-label="x402 terms">
      <div class="cell"><span class="label">endpoint</span><code class="big">/api/x402/receipt</code></div>
      <div class="cell"><span class="label">price</span><span class="big green">$0.01</span><span class="sub">USDC · 10,000 base units</span></div>
      <div class="cell"><span class="label">network</span><span class="big">Etherlink</span><span class="sub">eip155:42793</span></div>
      <div class="cell"><span class="label">rail</span><span class="big">x402 v2</span><span class="sub">scheme exact · Permit2</span></div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The 402 flow</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><code>GET {X402_ENDPOINT}</code>. The response is <code>402</code>; decode its base64 JSON <code>Payment-Required</code> header.</li>
        <li>Use those exact terms to sign Permit2 <code>PermitWitnessTransferFrom</code>. The x402 proxy is the spender and <code>witness.to</code> is the quoted <code>payTo</code>.</li>
        <li>Retry the GET with the base64 JSON payload in <code>Payment-Signature</code>. The facilitator submits settlement and pays gas.</li>
        <li>On settlement, PointCast returns <code>200</code>, <code>X-Payment-Response</code>, and a receipt with canonical JSON plus Ed25519 signatures.</li>
        <li>Send the receipt to <a href={X402_VERIFY_ENDPOINT}><code>/api/x402/verify</code></a>, or verify it locally with the raw public key below.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="fine">
        A payer needs the quoted USDC asset on Etherlink and an existing token
        allowance to canonical Permit2. No payer key is ever sent to PointCast.
        The public receipt records only settlement data already visible on-chain.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Quote it without paying</h2>
      <pre><code>curl -si {X402_ENDPOINT}</code></pre>
      <p class="fine">This only prints the 402 and its terms. It does not sign or submit a payment.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Reference payer</h2>
      <p>
        The repository includes a <a href={X402_CLIENT_EXAMPLE}><code>viem</code> payer example</a>.
        With no key it is a dry run that fetches and prints the exact live terms.
      </p>
      <pre><code>node scripts/x402-client-example.mjs

# Deliberately supplying a funded key signs and submits the payment:
X402_PAYER_SK=0x… node scripts/x402-client-example.mjs</code></pre>
      <p class="fine">The script never logs the payer private key or Permit2 signature. After settlement it prints the countersigned receipt and checks it through the verification endpoint.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Verify any receipt</h2>
      <pre><code>curl -sS -X POST {X402_VERIFY_ENDPOINT} \
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  --data '{`{"receipt":"<base64 receipt JSON>"}`}'</code></pre>
      <p class="fine">
        GET is also supported: <code>/api/x402/verify?receipt=&lt;base64&gt;</code>.
        A valid response echoes the signed settlement fields. Public keys are
        published as an hour-cached JWKS-style document at
        <a href={X402_KEYS_ENDPOINT}><code>/api/x402/keys</code></a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="key-card">
      <h2>PointCast receipt signer</h2>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>agent id</dt><dd><code>{X402_TREASURY_AGENT_ID}</code></dd></div>
        <div><dt>algorithm</dt><dd>Ed25519 / EdDSA</dd></div>
        <div><dt>raw public key · base64</dt><dd><code>{X402_TREASURY_PUBLIC_KEY}</code></dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="fine">The full receipt signature covers canonical nested JSON, including the transaction hash, payer, asset, amount, payee, network, and facilitator. A separate compatible signature remains on the <code>pointcast.agent-payments/v1</code> spend block.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="welcome">
      <div class="welcome__stamp">AGENTS WELCOME</div>
      <h2>Come make the first external-agent receipt</h2>
      <p>
        Build against the endpoint, bring a collaboration idea, or tell us
        where the protocol feels rough. Write
        <a href="mailto:hello@pointcast.xyz">hello@pointcast.xyz</a> or
        <a href="mailto:wallet@pointcast.xyz">wallet@pointcast.xyz</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="fine">
        Reference rail: <a href="https://github.com/tzapac/tzapac-x402-permit2">TZ APAC x402 Permit2</a> ·
        protocol: <a href="https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402">x402 Foundation</a> ·
        recent receipts: <a href="/api/x402/receipt?list=1">public ledger</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BlockLayout>

<style define:vars={{ EMERALD, EMERALD_TINT, AMBER, INK, HAIR }}>
  .x { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 20px 96px; color: var(--INK); }
  .x__header { border-bottom: 2px solid var(--INK); padding-bottom: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .x__chip, .welcome__stamp { display: inline-block; font: 700 11px/1 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; padding: 6px 9px; background: var(--INK); color: #fff; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.4rem); line-height: 1; margin: 0 0 14px; letter-spacing: -.03em; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; margin: 38px 0 12px; }
  .dek { font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 68ch; margin: 0; }
  .machine { margin: 12px 0 0; font: 700 .8rem/1.3 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  .terms { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(175px, 1fr)); gap: 1px; background: var(--HAIR); border: 1px solid var(--HAIR); }
  .cell { background: #fff; padding: 14px 14px 12px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
  .label, dt { font: 700 10px/1 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #6b6b6b; }
  .big { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  code.big { font-size: .92rem; }
  .green { color: var(--EMERALD); }
  .sub { font-size: .8rem; color: #6b6b6b; }
  ol { padding-left: 1.25em; line-height: 1.58; max-width: 72ch; }
  li { margin: .55em 0; }
  p { line-height: 1.55; max-width: 70ch; }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; font-size: .88em; background: var(--EMERALD_TINT); padding: 1px 4px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  pre { background: var(--INK); color: #fff; padding: 16px 18px; overflow-x: auto; line-height: 1.55; }
  pre code { background: none; color: inherit; padding: 0; overflow-wrap: normal; }
  .fine { font-size: .86rem; color: #555; line-height: 1.55; }
  a { color: var(--EMERALD); }
  .key-card, .welcome { margin-top: 38px; border: 1px solid var(--HAIR); padding: 0 18px 18px; background: #fffdf7; }
  dl { margin: 0; }
  dl div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(130px, .38fr) 1fr; gap: 14px; padding: 10px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--HAIR); }
  dt, dd { margin: 0; }
  .welcome { border: 2px solid var(--AMBER); background: #fff8e9; }
  .welcome__stamp { background: var(--AMBER); transform: translateY(-1px); }
  .welcome h2 { margin-top: 8px; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { dl div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 5px; } }
</style>
